From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: ROG5 reject modes above the core clock at the full pixel clock

dpu_crtc_mode_valid() halves the mode clock when the SoC has 3D merge,
while 0099 makes a video-mode interface vote the core clock for the full
pixel clock. Modes between the two limits were offered and then clamped to
the 460 MHz SM8350 maximum: on the MSI MPG 491C, 5120x1440@60 (469 MHz)
and 3840x1080@100 (453 MHz, x1.05 clk factor = 476 MHz) both showed only
the underflow colour (blue): with 1-2 % or no margin over the 460 MHz core
clock every frame underran (the debugfs counter merely stops counting once
the encoder IRQs are off after the idle timeout, so it looked latched), while
3840x1080@60 (266.5 MHz, +73 %) works.

Validate against the full pixel clock, as the vote does. With the 105%
factor this rejects pixel clocks above ~438 MHz; the DSI panel (command
mode, ~180 MHz) is unaffected. Suggested by GPT-6.1-Sol's review
(docs/reviews/2026-09-30-gpt-6.1-sol-open-issues.md).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1637,8 +1637,13 @@
 	adjusted_mode_clk = dpu_core_perf_adjusted_mode_clk(mode->clock,
 							    dpu_kms->perf.perf_cfg);
 
-	if (dpu_kms->catalog->caps->has_3d_merge)
-		adjusted_mode_clk /= 2;
+	/*
+	 * ROG5: no halving for 3D merge. A video-mode interface (DP) votes the
+	 * core clock for the full pixel clock (0099), so a mode above the max
+	 * core clock / clk factor was offered but could not be driven:
+	 * 5120x1440@60 (469 MHz) and 3840x1080@100 (453 MHz) on a 460 MHz
+	 * SM8350 underran on every frame (blue: 1-2 % or no clock margin).
+	 */
 
 	/*
 	 * The given mode, adjusted for the perf clock factor, should not exceed
